# 3. UNIVERSAL DOCUMENT ANALYSIS ENGINE

This is the most important product feature.

When a user uploads a supported file, DOCULENS must:

1. Receive the file.
2. Validate the file.
3. Extract the available content.
4. Detect whether OCR is required.
5. Classify the document.
6. Identify the issuing organization and document purpose where possible.
7. Extract all relevant facts.
8. Activate the correct analysis template.
9. Analyze all pages and sections.
10. Identify missing information.
11. Generate relevant checklists.
12. Generate action items.
13. Provide page-level source references.
14. Present the results in structured tabs and sub-tabs.

The system must not provide only a summary.

## GENERAL INFORMATION TO EXTRACT FROM EVERY DOCUMENT

Where applicable, identify:

- Document title.
- Document type.
- Document purpose.
- Issuing organization.
- Author or publisher.
- Recipient or intended audience.
- Document/reference number.
- Publication date.
- Effective date.
- Expiry date.
- Relevant jurisdiction.
- Main subject.
- Important parties.
- Monetary values.
- Important dates.
- Mandatory requirements.
- Optional requirements.
- Conditions.
- Responsibilities.
- Risks.
- Penalties.
- Important definitions.
- Required actions.
- Contact details.
- Official links.
- Annexures and references.

Not every field applies to every document.

Use "Not specified in the document" when information is absent.

Never invent a source, issuing organization, deadline, amount or eligibility condition.

